── Warning ('test-phase18-truncated-nbinom2-mu-random-intercept.R:143:3'): Phase 18 truncated NB2 mu random-intercept fit handles factors and missing rows ──
`drmTMB()`: the fitted `log(sigma)` spans 11.5 across observations, more than `log(1e4)` = 9.2.
i A scale range wider than 10^4 usually means the scale is running off (or the design is extreme), so the reported convergence, estimates and standard errors may be unreliable even when the clamp is not hit. Rescale the response, simplify the `sigma` formula, or use a penalized/MAP fit; `check_drm()` reports the fit state.
