── Warning ('test-start-contract.R:311:3'): a fixef:sigma: start outside the log-sigma clamp band warns instead of silently reporting a clean convergence (defect A2-D1) ──
`drmTMB()`: the `log(sigma)` clamp is active at the optimum (the fitted `log(sigma)` reached 15, above the band upper bound 12).
i The scale ran to the upper clamp, so the fit may have converged artificially: estimates and standard errors near the clamp are unreliable. Rescale the response, widen the band with `drm_control(logsigma_clamp = )`, add within-group replication, or use a penalized/MAP fit; `check_drm()` reports the fit state.
